    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92429" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥιζότομ-ος</span></b>  (parox.), ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who cuts</i> or
				<i>gathers roots</i>, esp. for purposes of medicine or
			witchcraft, <i>herbalist</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.1.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				9.8.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				<u>Prooem.</u>
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DDeor.</u>
				13.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥιζοτόμοι, αἱ</span>, title of play by Sophocles, <i><span class="en">
				Macr.
				<u>Sat.</u>
				5.19.9
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as
				Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. ὥρα</span> the
			time <i>for cutting roots</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				494
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ῥ.</span>, name of a kind of
			<i>iris</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				21.41
			</span></i>.</div>
